## Baseline

B is the context of a session's first call (input + cache read + cache creation): exact. Every call re-reads it, so its token-turns share is B × N / Σ context over the session's N calls.

**Pooled share (headline): 89.1%** of all input read by the 5 eligible main sessions is the fixed baseline. Typical session: 92.0% (median of per-session shares, median N = 4; this mostly reflects session length).

| Sessions | n | B p50 | B p90 | Pooled share | Typical session | Median N |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| main | 5 | 5,000 | — | 89.1% | 92.0% | 4 |
| subagent (fixed overhead + task prompt) | 1 | 800 | — | 88.9% | 88.9% | 3 |

B p90 is printed only from 10 sessions.

Artifact is carried in 1 of 1 subagent tool snapshots; main-session levers also shrink subagent baselines.

